From b522d95e922c5c17e508e1ebb9f9a2bf58d3d3ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somesh Velupally <somegupt@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:48:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] refactor(qti-accesscontrol): restructure XPU3/VMIDMT
 driver into layered cfg/ layout

Restructure drivers/qti/accesscontrol/ to separate hardware driver
sources from per-SoC compile-time policy tables, making it easier to
support multiple XPU hardware revisions without touching every layer:

- xpu3/xpu3_hal.c, xpu3_hal.h: XPU3 register-level programming
  extracted into a dedicated HAL layer
- xpu3/xpu3_hwio.h: XPU3 register offset definitions
- xpu3/xpu3_isr.c: violation reporting and interrupt registration,
  split out from access_control.c
- xpu3/xpu3.c, xpu3.h: revision driver implementing xpu_common.h
- xpu_common.h: revision-agnostic interface keeping access_control.c
  revision-neutral
- vmidmt/vmidmt_cfg.h: configuration provider interface; one provider
  linked per build, supplied by cfg/${CHIPSET}
- vmidmt/vmidmt_internal.h: wire-format structs with CASSERT layout
  assertions pinning field offsets
- vmidmt/vmidmt.c: restructured to a per-instance configure_masters()
  pass; per-instance vmid_map tables replace the flat global g_vmid_map[]
- cfg/<chipset>/: compile-time policy tables per SoC; kodiak and lemans
  migrated from vmidmt/<chipset>/ and xpu/<chipset>/ with policy values
  unchanged
- access_control.mk: updated to reflect the new layout

Change-Id: I68b55cd22d24e246a9033bbcc4e2b08a79374491
